---
import Prose from "../layouts/Prose.astro";
import { contactEmail } from "../config";

const email = contactEmail();
---
<Prose title="Privacy">
  <p class="mt-4">
    Road to Sixty is run by <a href="https://jordanburch.dev">Jordan Burch</a>. This page says what it keeps about you, where, and how to have it
    removed. In short: only what syncing needs, nothing public, nothing sold.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The addon on its own</h2>
    <p>The addon saves everything in your own World of Warcraft folder. Nothing leaves your computer unless you install the app and link it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the app sends</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your BattleTag, to show which account a PC is linked to.</li>
      <li>Your Battle.net account number, scrambled with a secret key before it is stored, so the number itself is never kept.</li>
      <li>Each character's name, realm and journey: where it went, quests, kills, levels, gear, and the names of other players it grouped with.</li>
      <li>For each linked PC: the name you gave it, whether it's a Mac or Windows, and its app and addon versions.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where it's kept</h2>
    <p>Accounts and the list of versions are in a database on a server Jordan runs. Journey files are in Cloudflare R2 storage. Database backups are deleted after 30 days.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>Only you, through the app on a PC you linked. Nothing is shown publicly, and nothing is sold or shared with anyone.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Deleting it</h2>
    <p>
      In the app, open Account and choose Delete everything. Your account and every journey are removed from the server at once, and from backups
      within 30 days. Journeys on your own PCs stay. You can download everything first, from the same screen.
    </p>
    <p>You can also ask by email at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>, for a copy, a correction or deletion.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>This site sets none. The sign-in page on the sync server sets one when you link a PC. Only that page uses it, and it expires within a week.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Battle.net</h2>
    <p>
      Signing in goes through Blizzard's Battle.net. Road to Sixty only receives your account number and BattleTag, never your password. Road to
      Sixty isn't affiliated with Blizzard Entertainment.
    </p>
  </section>
</Prose>
